{"content":[{"c":["NETHANEEL*, NETHANEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common OT name spelled Nethaneel in the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Zuar’s son and the prince of Issachar’s tribe at the start of Israel’s wilderness wanderings (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.8","r":"Num.1.8","rawR":"Num.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.8","value":"Num.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.5","r":"Num.2.5","rawR":"Num.2.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.5","value":"Num.2.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.15","r":"Num.10.15","rawR":"Num.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.15","value":"Num.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:15"},"), who represented his kinsmen at the altar’s dedication (",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.18,23","r":"Num.7.18,23","rawR":"Num.7.18,23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.18,23","value":"Num.7.18,23"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:18, 23"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Judahite, the fourth son of Jesse and David’s brother (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.14","r":"1Chr.2.14","rawR":"1Chr.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.14","value":"1Chr.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. One of the priests assigned to blow a trumpet before the ark in the procession led by David when the ark was moved to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.24","r":"1Chr.15.24","rawR":"1Chr.15.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.24","value":"1Chr.15.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Levite and the father of Shemaiah, the scribe who recorded the 24 divisions of priests founded during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.6","r":"1Chr.24.6","rawR":"1Chr.24.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.6","value":"1Chr.24.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Korahite Levite and Obed-edom’s fifth son in David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.4","r":"1Chr.26.4","rawR":"1Chr.26.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.4","value":"1Chr.26.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. One of the princes sent by King Jehoshaphat to teach the law in the cities of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.7","r":"2Chr.17.7","rawR":"2Chr.17.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.7","value":"2Chr.17.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. One of the Levitical chiefs who generously gave animals to the Levites for the celebration of the Passover feast during King Josiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.9","r":"2Chr.35.9","rawR":"2Chr.35.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.9","value":"2Chr.35.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Priest and one of Pashhur’s six sons who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.22","r":"Ezra.10.22","rawR":"Ezra.10.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.22","value":"Ezra.10.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Head of Jedaiah’s priestly family during the days of Joiakim, the high priest, in postexilic Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.21","r":"Neh.12.21","rawR":"Neh.12.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.21","value":"Neh.12.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the priestly musicians who performed at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall during Nehemiah’s day (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.36","r":"Neh.12.36","rawR":"Neh.12.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.36","value":"Neh.12.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"NethaneelNethanel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 1:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.8","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.8","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.8"},{"anchorText":"2:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.5","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.5","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.5"},{"anchorText":"10:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.15","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.15","sourceRefExact":"Num.10.15"},{"anchorText":"7:18, 23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.7.18,23","rawQueryValue":"Num.7.18,23","sourceRefExact":"Num.7.18,23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.14","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.14","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.14"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.24","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.24","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 17:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.17.7","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.17.7","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.17.7"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 35:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.35.9","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.35.9","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.35.9"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.22","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.22","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.22"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.21","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.21","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.21"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:36","canonicalization":"deferred_